+# Decisions Log — Memory Injection Ranker (a5ecc5aa)
+
+## 2026-07-24 · Task 0 (capture-side precondition) — BLOCKING FINDING
+
+**Verdict: STOP the ranker build. The precondition failed — the memory corpus is empty.**
+
+Query (read-only, prod Neon) via `apps/platform-api/scripts/capture-check.mjs`:
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `memories` total (any status) | **0** |
+| `memories` by status | **[]** (no rows at all) |
+| active decisions/facts | 0 |
+| active rules | 0 |
+| tenants with memories | 0 |
+| `agent_runs` total | 7 (newest 4.6 days old) |
+
+**Interpretation.** The store is not thin — it is empty. This is not a Review-Inbox/approval
+bottleneck (there are zero *proposed* memories either). Nothing is being captured. Per the issue's own
+Fable-pass mandate ("a small store means capture, not ranking, is the real bottleneck"), the ranking work
+(a5ecc5aa) is **premature**: a relevance ranker over an empty corpus has zero observable effect, and the
+Task 1 offline query-construction experiment is infeasible (7 runs, 0 captured memories to replay).
+
+**The real bottleneck is CAPTURE.** No memories exist despite 7 agent runs. Candidates for *why*:
+- Reflection engine has no autonomous trigger (issue **3ecc1859**) — nothing runs it.
+- Memory-capture-on-accept (#132) may not have fired (no work-item accepts) or may not be wired to these
+  runs — **to be verified**.
+
+**Decision:** do not proceed to Phase 1 shadow code or Task 1. Resequence: land capture first (make
+memories actually get created), re-run this exact capture check, and only then resume the ranker — its
+shadow-first design is still correct, just blocked on a non-empty store.
+
+**a5ecc5aa status:** blocked on capture. Kept open with this finding recorded; not closed (the ranker is
+still the right eventual fix, just not now).
+
+**Artifacts:** `apps/platform-api/scripts/capture-check.mjs` (reusable precondition check — re-run after
+capture lands to confirm the store is non-empty before resuming).
